        "original_id": "fcb9c1be-b493-5f3f-a98f-2b3a4dce17cb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 2013 Sydney to Hobart Yacht Race\n- Places: Sydney Harbour, Tasman Sea, Bass Strait, Storm Bay, River Derwent, Hobart, Tasmania, United Kingdom\n- Topics: Boxing Day, holidays, British Empire\n\nFacts:\n- Boxing Day is a holiday celebrated the day after Christmas Day.\n- Boxing Day originated in the United Kingdom and is celebrated in a number of countries that previously formed part of the British Empire.\n- The 2013 Sydney to Hobart Yacht Race began on Sydney Harbour at 1pm on Boxing Day, 26 December 2013.\n- The 2013 Sydney to Hobart Yacht Race covered 630 nautical miles through the Tasman Sea, past Bass Strait, into Storm Bay and up the River Derwent to finish in Hobart, Tasmania.",
